# Normalize line endings across the repo: LF in working copies,
# CRLF in the index for the legacy CRLF-preserved DOS-style files
# already in git history. New Python/TOML/Markdown/YAML files should
# be added with the `text` attribute below.
#
# Background: this project has a long history on Windows + various
# IDEs mixing LF and CRLF. We don't want to rewrite history on every
# clone, so we tell git:
#   * for ALL text files, work in LF locally;
#   * keep the on-disk content of legacy CRLF files as CRLF in the
#     index so existing clones don't churn.

# Defaults: every text file uses LF in working copy; git autoclf cleans
# the rest.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Force CRLF on these legacy files (already CRLF in the index).
*.py text eol=crlf
*.toml text eol=crlf
.gitignore text eol=lf
.github/workflows/*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Treat everything below as binary so no conversions ever happen.
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
*.pst binary
*.ost binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
